    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and it passes. The change is complete and the suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the \"reject duplicate lower-cased email with 409\" rule for `POST /api/owners`, following the existing telephone/household uniqueness pattern rather than inventing a new shape:\n\n- **`EnsureUniqueEmail.java`** (new function) \u2014 reads the already-normalized request email; skips when absent/blank (email is optional); rejects with `DuplicateEmailException` if any existing owner's lower-cased email matches. Reuses the existing `EmailNormalizer.normalize` so create/stored comparison stays consistent.\n- **`DuplicateEmailException.java`** (new checked exception) \u2014 mirrors `DuplicateTelephoneException`.\n- **`DuplicateEmailExceptionHandler.java`** (new escalation handler) \u2014 responds `409 CONFLICT` with `{\"error\": \"...\"}`, mirroring the telephone handler.\n- **`...DuplicateEmailException.yml`** (new escalation wiring).\n- **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 inserted an `ensureUniqueEmail` step right after `normalizeEmail` (so it runs on the canonical lower-cased value) and before `ensureUniqueTelephone`/`build`, under `govern: [ transaction ]` like the sibling checks, so a collision is rejected before any owner is built or saved.\n\nEach piece has a single responsibility and reuses existing helpers (`EmailNormalizer`, the escalation/handler convention). Full test suite: **BUILD SUCCESS**, 1/1 passing.",
